{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:46:36Z","thinking":"**Preparing to draft lemmas**\n\nPlan is to write lemmas and proof in `scratch.lean`. The elaboration time might be around 6-8 seconds, therefore the time to wait for synchronous elaboration will be set to 10 seconds. Now I'll start testing by writing a lemma.\n\n\n**Developing the proof strategy**\n\nAttempting to construct a proof using `Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn` by defining a function `choice_e` that maps each vertex in the independent set to an edge in the edge cover. The `MapsTo` condition holds trivially. The `InjOn` condition, stating that the mapping is injective, is being investigated. The goal is to show `choice_e u = choice_e v → u = v`. If `u` and `v` belong to the same edge `e`, and `u ≠ v`, then `e` is necessarily the edge containing `u` and `v` which implies that the edge is uniquely defined. Now, searching in Mathlib for `Sym2.eq_of_ne_mem` or similar lemmas.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen Finset SimpleGraph\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V)\n\n#check (Sym2.mem_iff : ∀ {a b c : V}, a ∈ s(b, c) ↔ a = b ∨ a = c)\n\nexample (u v : V) (e : Sym2 V) (hu : u ∈ e) (hv : v ∈ e) (hne : u ≠ v) : e = s(u, v) := by\n  induction e using Sym2.inductionOn with\n  | h a b =>\n    rw [Sym2.mem_iff] at hu hv\n    rcases hu with rfl | rfl <;> rcases hv with rfl | rfl\n    · contradiction\n    · rfl\n    · exact Sym2.eq_swap\n    · contradiction\n\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\n","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_1facfd37","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing Sym2 equality in scratch.lean","toolSummary":"Test Sym2 induction in scratch.lean"}}]}
